<!--CLI Capability — GenerateAgentsMd
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.capability.GenerateAgentsMd-->
<clicap:GenerateAgentsMd xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clicommand="org.blockml.bml.cli.command"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    core:Capability
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Rewrite AGENTS.md from AgentInstructions blocks
  </is>
  <documentation>
    <![CDATA[
    # Rewrite AGENTS.md from AgentInstructions blocks

    Public entry generateAgentsMd({ rootDir, srcDir? }) → { code, lines, sectionCount }.
    sectionCount is the number of sections plus rules.
    blockml agents-md generate parses flags, calls this capability, and prints lines.
    blockml init calls it after npm install unless noInstall.
    Init preflight renames a foreign AGENTS.md to AGENTS.md.pre-blockml
    before that call when package.json has no blockml key. When the key is
    present, this capability overwrites AGENTS.md.
    --no-install skips that call. Preflight still runs.

    Corpus is the project source folder plus the blocks roots of direct
    dependencies and devDependencies. A dependency counts when its package.json
    declares blockml.library or it has blockml.config.json. Resolution is
    node_modules/<name> from the project root upward. optionalDependencies
    and transitive dependencies are not searched. This is not the validate --all
    corpus and does not follow Library dependencies.

    A block is included when its baseType chain contains
    org.blockml.bml.core.AgentInstructions and the block is not that type.
    order is the authored integer, otherwise the inherited property default
    (1000). sections and rules are two streams. Each stream sorts blocks by
    order ascending, then FQN ascending. Children of one aggregation stay in
    document order. Every section is emitted before any rule.

    Every section heading is level 1. Body text is the section content with
    trailing whitespace removed. rules then become one level-1 heading taken
    from the aggregation name (rules → Rules). Each rule is a markdown list
    item. The file is <root>/AGENTS.md.

    At least one section or rule → overwrite AGENTS.md, code 0.
    Neither → code 1, and an existing AGENTS.md stays unchanged.
    ]]>
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:AgentsMdCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicommand:AgentsMdCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicap:InitProject" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
  <properties>
    <rootDir type="type:Text">
      <documentation>
        Project root. package.json and AGENTS.md live here. (required)
      </documentation>
    </rootDir>
    <srcDir type="type:Text">
      <documentation>
        Project source folder. Default blocks. (optional)
      </documentation>
    </srcDir>
  </properties>
</clicap:GenerateAgentsMd>
